{# These templates cater for 3 use cases:

1. Bodybuilder matrix block types
2. CKEditor embedded entries
3. Reusable widget entries inserted via the bodybuilder matrix - routed through widgetBlock.twig just like any other block type.

The default is for CKEditor embedded entries (because the routing there is fully automatic and we have no opportunity to add our own parameters). You can then differentiate with `owner` or `field`, or by passing through a parameter in bodyBuilder.twig to decide whether to apply wrapping or whatever else needs to change. E.g. {{ entry.field and entry.field.handle == 'body' ? 'Inside CKEditor' : 'Inside Bodybuilder' }}. Using `owner` could be a bit trickier as technically you could be inside a CKE inside a bodybuilder matrix (though try to minimise that use case as complexity will soon blossom!!).

If #1 and #2 are likely to be very different from each other, you might consider using this template as a router to fork into two different sub templates. Name them with underscores as exampleBlock_something.twig and exampleBlock_somethingElse.twig to maintain proximity in a list. Do not use nested sub directories. Usually though it's enough to simply wrap/unwrap the container partial according to whether you're in #1 or #2. Use `set...endset` to create an `innards` variable which you can then easily apply inside/outside a container.

Be sure to conditionally show/hide fields in Craft that are only relevant to one or more of the use cases - typically using the "`field`... is one of ... bodybuilder" condition. Beware that widget entries should not choose their own background colours - that is delegated to the bodybuilder block.

#}